<python>
cs_content_header = "Welcome to ECO 101 — Introduction to Economics"
</python>

<h2>About This Course</h2>
<p><strong>ECO 101: Introduction to Economics</strong> provides students with foundational knowledge in both microeconomics and macroeconomics. You will learn how individuals, firms, and governments make decisions under conditions of scarcity, how markets operate, and how the Nigerian and global economies function.</p>

<p>No prior economics knowledge is required. All that is needed is curiosity and a willingness to think critically about the world around you.</p>

<h2>What You Will Learn</h2>
<ul>
  <li>The law of demand and supply, and how prices are determined in markets</li>
  <li>Consumer behaviour and utility theory</li>
  <li>Production costs and firm behaviour</li>
  <li>Market structures: perfect competition, monopoly, and oligopoly</li>
  <li>National income accounting: GDP, inflation, and unemployment</li>
  <li>Monetary and fiscal policy tools</li>
  <li>International trade and Nigeria's role in the global economy</li>
</ul>

<h2>Weekly Topics</h2>

* [Week 1: Law of Demand and Supply](Econs/week1)


